	<p>This mountain is part of the Nounou Mountain range, commonly known as
the <q>Sleeping Giant</q> due to its distinctive profile that
resembles a reclining giant. This range is a prominent feature on the
east side of Kaua'i, offering stunning views and popular hiking
trails. The lush greenery covering the cliffs is a result of the
island's abundant rainfall, which promotes the dense tropical
vegetation.</p>
	<img src='20240525_144536.jpg' />

	<p>I'd be lying if I said I wasn't hurting by the time we got home (did
I mention the upcoming hip transplant?) but I was promised a day off
tomorrow. And meanwhile, there's the sound of surf and the absolutely
clean sea air and the rising moon to comfort me.</p>
